LIBRARY

Open the data file matching its category — e.g. `data/library/articles.yaml`.

2. Add a new block:
   ```yaml

# - title: ""
#   url: ""
#   category: ""
#   subcategory: ""
#   note: ""

   ```
3. To add a **brand-new category**, create a new file `data/library/your-category-name.yaml` with the same structure. A checkbox and section heading for it will appear automatically — no template edits needed.

---

## Chronological history

**1. Initial build** — created the filtering system from scratch:
- `data/library.yaml` (single flat file) — 6 entries migrated from old freeform Markdown, each with `title`/`url`/`category`/`note`
- `content/library.md` — simplified to front-matter-only, added `layout = "library"`
- `layouts/_default/library.html` — new template: sidebar with search box + auto-generated category checkboxes (derived from data, not hand-maintained), main area with entries grouped by category, vanilla-JS filter (search + checkboxes combine with AND logic, empty groups auto-hide)
- `layouts/partials/style.html` — added `.library`, `.library-sidebar`, `.library-search`, `.library-filter-list`, `.library-content`, `.library-group`, `.library-item`, `.library-no-results`, plus a mobile breakpoint stacking the sidebar above content under 600px

**2. Fixed a deprecation warning** — `.Site.Data.library` → `(hugo.Data).library` (Hugo deprecated the old syntax).

**3. Removed dead CSS** — `#search`, `.resource-group`, `.resource-grid`, `.resource-item` rules deleted from `style.html`. These were leftovers from the old `layouts/resources/list.html` (deleted earlier, in a separate task) and had nothing left referencing them.

**4. Incident: `content/library.md` was deleted** (by you, assuming it was redundant now that entries live in the data file) — this broke the `/library` route entirely, since that file's front matter is what tells Hugo to create the page and which template to use. You reinstated it with the original front matter; page confirmed working again.

**5. Split the data file for scalability** — in preparation for "hundreds of links":
- Deleted `data/library.yaml`
- Created `data/library/calculators-and-platforms.yaml` and `data/library/articles.yaml` (same 6 entries, same content, just divided by category into separate files)
- Updated `layouts/_default/library.html`: the data-loading step now flattens `hugo.Data.library` (a map of `{filename: [entries]}`) back into a single list before the existing grouping/search/checkbox logic runs — so nothing downstream needed to change.


Everything for the newsletter form lives in **one file: `layouts/partials/newsletter-form.html`**. There's a clearly marked block inside it:

```html
<!-- ============================================================
     EDIT HERE to rename lists or add/remove one.
     ...
     ============================================================ -->
<fieldset class="newsletter-lists">
    ...
</fieldset>
<!-- ============================================================ -->
```

To rename a list, just change its visible text (e.g. `Offerings` → `Products`) — no need to touch the `name` attribute unless you also want to rename it on the backend side later. To add a 4th list, copy one of the `<label class="newsletter-list-option">...</label>` blocks and give it a unique `name`.

**What I implemented:**
- Nothing is pre-checked by default (visitors actively opt in to whichever they want).
- "All of it" is a pure UI convenience — checking it auto-checks Blog/Podcast/Offerings (and unchecking any individual one un-checks "All of it"); it submits no value of its own.
- Submission isn't blocked if nothing's checked — reasonable for now since the form has no real backend yet (`action="#"` placeholder still in place).
- Styling kept compact and self-contained in the existing `.newsletter-*` CSS section in `layouts/partials/style.html`.

**Validation:** `hugo --cleanDestinationDir` built clean (38 pages, no errors), and confirmed via `grep` that all four checkboxes render with correct attributes.
